      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KIWI HARMONY (5) was out of the money two runs back then again missed the frame last start over 1400m at Coffs Harbour, beaten a length into fifth. Well placed and should be there at the finish. IRISH ACCOLADE (4) improved last start but found one better over 1400m at Gunnedah, beaten less than a length. Has the class to figure prominently. SO SAIN (8) has been well supported in her two runs back but has only managed midfield finishes. Strips fitter third-up and may be worth one more chance out to this distance. NARUKAMI (7) wasn't as bad second-up at the Gold Coast when finishing fifth. This isn't a deep maiden, so should could surprise. Debutant ASTRIDANE (1) best of the rest.",
